  "notes": "Breakshot gameplay check on fresh isolated state. Three balls in the trough (36-38 at 1); two coins and Start begin a game and the served ball passes the shooter lane (43). With every target standing, each flipper input is held in turn (the flipper column's left and right button bits 84 and 82, the ROM's UR. FLIPPER switch 21, and the column's lower-right end-of-stroke bit 81, which CAPCOM.VBS writes for a staged right flipper key) to show which flipper coils each one fires. Then public 48 goes to 1 alone as a control, the right drop bank goes down as 49-51 and then as 48-50, and the left bank goes down as 73-75; the DMD's drop-target animation and score show which addresses the ROM scores as bank targets. Last, the tilt bob (30) is touched three times and the slam tilt (29) once, and the DMD shows the ROM's response to each.",
